WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.687
Here's what the register holds.

2
00:00:01.687 --> 00:00:05.378
The public name is a public
IP's DNS name and address,

3
00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:10.825
a Front Door profile's custom domains,
or an application gateway's public IP.

4
00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:12.688
The owner is the owner tag.

5
00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:16.726
The DDoS column is the IP's protection
mode, or "Front Door edge",

6
00:00:16.726 --> 00:00:22.138
because Learn says Front Door's edge has
built-in layer three and four protection.

7
00:00:22.138 --> 00:00:25.687
And the WAF columns name
the policy and its mode.

8
00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:29.167
Five rules read it: a row
without an owner is a finding;

9
00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:32.080
a public IP attached to
nothing is a warning;

10
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.751
a new row since last week is information;

11
00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:38.473
a row that went away is a
warning to check its DNS records;

12
00:00:38.473 --> 00:00:43.870
and an exposure Defender reports that the
register lacks is a gap in the queries.
